              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Diane H"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Do not mix with mixer!! Original recipe was not submitted that way. Mix all ingredients by hand just until all ingredients are blended. No bake pie is ready in only 15 minutes. I know, I sent the recipe in! Enjoy!"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "4"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "SDSMarvin"
            },
            "reviewBody": "The original recipe is good. I used white chocolate pudding instead of the vanilla and be careful with sour cream. Mix the pineapple, pudding, and sugar first. Then fold in the sour cream, if you mix to much the sour cream will brake down and make your pie runny.",
            "datePublished": "2011-07-17T10:38:13.910Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "SColson782"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Forget about the crust! I enjoyed this as a fluff. I used sugar-free pudding and Splenda. I am a diabetic. Delicioso!",
            "datePublished": "2021-10-22T14:09:14.570Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "JackiG"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Delightful cream pie! I added a layer of sliced strawberries on the bottom of the crust, then added the filling. Topped with whipped cream and a nice thick layer of coconut. Thanks for sharing!",
            "datePublished": "2020-05-31T01:21:57.050Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Cindy Witt"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I made individual \"pies\" using my mini muffin pan and mini cupcake papers. I used the graham cracker crust from this site for the base, baked for 7 minutes and removed from the pan to cool. Then I piped the filling into the cups. I also mixed everything by hand and had no problems with runniness. Great recipe!",
            "datePublished": "2011-02-05T18:14:46.757Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Tracy Tyler"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Fast easy and yummy. I made it in a graham cracker crust added a small amount of natural orange flavoring and orange food coloring colored some coconut blue and orange to make a Denver Broncos orange crush pie for our tailgate party. It was a hit my husband really liked it.",
            "datePublished": "2021-10-02T06:22:23.057Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "4"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Trillian"
            },
            "reviewBody": "This is a great recipe! I don't like using packaged and processed vanilla pudding mix, so I used the \"Homemade Vanilla Pudding\" recipe on AR, and in that recipe I substitute dry milk powder for fresh milk, the vanilla powder for vanilla extract and omit the butter. I have made this with fresh pineapple and canned, and prefer the fresh version. I also like this as a dessert custard and omit the crust to avoid a few calories! Thanks to Diana for clarifying the process to mix by hand and for a great recipe.",
            "datePublished": "2025-09-07T17:13:03.780Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Bloodshot"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I made this just now. However I did not measure my pie plate. This might fill a store bought frozen pie shell, but because of my error it looked a little empty in my 10 inch plate with an unrolled premade crust. Next time I'll double the ingredients. It tastes great, though. And I did as others have and mixed it by hand. Really, with these soft ingredients, there is no reason to get out a mixer.",
            "datePublished": "2022-04-15T23:09:28.363Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "4"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "jk mcfarland"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Trying to do keto, so I used sugar free pudding. They come in .9 oz packages not 3.4 so I used 4 because my pie pan is deep dish. 20 oz crushed pineapple but still 1 cup sour cream. Probably could have used more sour cream but it set up nicely. Topped with whipped cream, sugar free and monk fruit sweetener. Nut flour for the Graham cracker crust. Not bad at all.",
            "datePublished": "2020-04-23T17:50:13.903Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Oh No Cook"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I followed the recipe but doubled it and made a graham cracker crust. It fit perfectly in a 9 1/2 deep dish pie plate with room for the whipped topping garnish. It was a hit at dinner and found that it was even better the next day. Nice and easy recipe.",
            "datePublished": "2018-05-14T02:04:43.580Z"
          },
          {
